  "necessity_paragraph": "The patient presents with intermittent palpitations and a known history of atherosclerotic heart disease of the native coronary artery (I25.10). Mobile cardiac telemetry (CPT 93229) is medically necessary to correlate these symptomatic episodes with underlying arrhythmias and to assess for ischemic changes in the context of the established coronary artery disease. The submitted clinical indication note documents the symptomatic episodes and the underlying diagnosis that support the use of this diagnostic modality."
